, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "866fab34e097e4b1bf4834e75d5556b53c74672d", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2023-06-18T16:32:39Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "845207d56b1f6655637f2db8be1379f5382951ca", "message": "Create printing_array.py", "created_at": "2023-06-18T16:20:50Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "34d0d2c3df1f307d78cf54d6870beabb06581b9f", "message": "Update kaden's.py", "created_at": "2023-06-18T15:23:38Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "5620b49192cb491ba9f8031af514ea9bdedeae0a", "message": "Create brute_force.py\n\nbrute force approach has time complexity of O(n^3 )approx", "created_at": "2023-06-18T15:00:14Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4b70e607a5a82f8b1e008d9f53b8a78a40faf4ac", "message": "Create n2.py", "created_at": "2023-06-18T14:38:28Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "143f0bfc6de85f1d5b49e2695aa1c21d3b340a87", "message": "Create kaden's.py", "created_at": "2023-06-18T14:36:36Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "cbbcc32d150abe6866061d9373291f6cd945ac42", "message": "Create assingment", "created_at": "2023-06-02T22:30:18Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "3bca3ed69a91f6df9ea893ed89697b6827716912", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2023-06-02T22:26:35Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ed7ea4613bf802c729677bc0119db90f15fc7643", "message": "Create README.md", "created_at": "2023-06-02T22:25:10Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "3d5f1879b34ff9b4987c550063fd893dade37c2a", "message": "Add files via upload\n\n## Problem 1 : Longest Stable Subsequence\r\n\r\nConsider a list of numbers $[a_0, a_1, \\cdots, a_{n-1}]$. Our goal is to find the the longest stable subsequence: $[a_{i_1}, a_{i_2}, \\cdots, a_{i_k} ]$ which is a sub-list of the original list that selects elements at indices $i_1, i_2, \\ldots, i_k$ from the original list such that \r\n  1. $i_1 < i_2 < \\cdots < i_k$; \r\n  2. $a_{i_{j+1}} - 1 \\leq a_{i_{j}} \\leq a_{i_{j+1}} + 1 $. We can also write this as $|a_{i_{j+1}} - a_{i_j}| \\leq 1$. I.e, each element of the subsequence must be within $\\pm 1$ or equal to the previous element.\r\n  3. The length of the subsequence $k$ is maximized.\r\n\r\n### Example \r\n\r\nConsider the list `[1, 4, 2, -2, 0, -1, 2, 3]`.  There are many \"stable subsequences\":\r\n - `[1, 0, -1]`\r\n - `[1, 2, 2, 3]`\r\n - `[4, 3]`\r\n\r\nThe longest stable subsequence is `[1, 2, 2, 3]` of length 4. Note that each element of the subsequence is at most $1$ away from the previous element.\r\n\r\nThe goal of this problem is to formulate a dynamic programming solution to find the length of the longest stable subsequence and the subsequence itself.", "created_at": "2023-06-02T22:22:23Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "c139d907900145e3ccd296dce206d776fd53a06b", "message": "max sub array", "created_at": "2023-05-11T17:22:31Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "d6cea6db0d9f485028544570194ef0d1c313349d", "message": "Delete main.class", "created_at": "2023-05-04T13:52:25Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "63b8dc83c23dfccc7665e0f967243c0904f458bb", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2023-05-04T13:51:21Z", "repo": "DSA-CHECK-LIST", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}], "prs": []}